    source('src-long-game-official', 'The Long Game', 'DoctorWho.tv', 'https://www.doctorwho.tv/stories/the-long-game', 'official_tv_synopsis_indexed', 'Public Satellite Five, promotion and manipulation synopsis read', 'Humanity’s news system is manipulated.', 'Information control is not automatic material provision.'),
    source('src-new-earth-reference', 'New Earth', 'Wikipedia contributors', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Earth_(Doctor_Who)', 'secondary_tv_plot_reference_indexed', 'Public hospital, infected clones and cure-spreading explanation read', 'A hospital derives treatments from living biological test subjects.', 'Powerful medicine and a cure do not establish automated care labor, free universal treatment or work-independent material access.'),
    source('src-gridlock-reference', 'Gridlock', 'Wikipedia contributors', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gridlock_(Doctor_Who)', 'secondary_tv_plot_reference_indexed', 'Public perpetual Motorway, surviving population and surface-virus passages read', 'A trapped population survives in vehicles after the surface city’s collapse.', 'The motorway cohort and earlier functioning city are different scopes. Mood drugs and a city name do not transfer New Earth hospital policies.'),
    source('src-gridlock-recycling-dialogue', 'Gridlock: Transcript', 'Episode dialogue transcribed by TARDIS Guide', 'https://tardis.guide/story/gridlock/transcript/', 'primary_tv_dialogue_transcription', 'Bounded lines 289-325, 333-341 and 473-509 read', 'Years of residence, self-replicating fuel, waste-to-food recycling and missing emergency institutions.', 'No whole transcript or new viewing. The source establishes ongoing survival equipment, not complete long-term medical care or a work census.'),
    source('src-beast-below-reference', 'The Beast Below', 'Wikipedia contributors', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Beast_Below', 'secondary_tv_plot_reference_indexed', 'Public Starship UK and coerced Star Whale propulsion explanation read', 'A colony ship’s movement relies on a biological whale.', 'Propulsion and behavioral control do not establish automatic household distribution, and the whale is not an AI.'),
    source('src-rebel-flesh-reference', 'The Rebel Flesh', 'Wikipedia contributors', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Flesh', 'secondary_tv_plot_reference_indexed', 'Public acid factory, remote avatars and their independence passages read', 'Workers initially control Gangers to perform hazardous industrial activity.', 'Remote human labor is not autonomous replacement; later independent persons do not automatically inherit a post-work support system.'),
    source('src-girl-waited-review', 'Doctor Who Recap: The Girl Who Waited', 'WIRED', 'https://www.wired.com/2011/09/doctor-who-recap-the-girl-who-waited', 'secondary_tv_recap_indexed', 'Public parallel time streams, handbots and species-specific plague passages read', 'A medical/quarantine setting has robotic care and distorted waiting times.', 'A treatment facility and an anomalous stranded patient do not establish the host society’s economic rules; no universal safe care is inferred.'),
    source('src-robots-death-official', 'The Robots of Death', 'DoctorWho.tv', 'https://www.doctorwho.tv/stories/the-robots-of-death', 'official_tv_synopsis_indexed', 'Public sandminer, small human crew and near-total robot dependence synopsis read', 'Robots do most shipboard tasks while a human crew mines minerals.', 'A highly automated productive workplace is not itself a resident population obtaining necessities independently of employment.'),
    source('src-ark-official', 'The Ark', 'DoctorWho.tv', 'https://www.doctorwho.tv/stories/the-ark', 'official_tv_synopsis_indexed', 'Public cold, time jump and reversed enslavement synopsis read', 'Human and Monoid power reverses during a generation-ship voyage.', 'Biological servants remain persons doing actual work; neither hierarchy establishes automatic labor replacement.'),
    source('src-ark-space-official-reference', 'The Ark in Space', 'Tom Baker Official', 'https://www.tombakerofficial.com/series/the-ark-in-space/', 'official_performer_story_reference_indexed', 'Public automated Nerva, selected sleepers and Wirrn threat synopsis read', 'An automated station preserves selected sleeping humans.', 'Preservation is not an awake leisure society, and a future resettlement plan is not an established distribution system.'),
    source('src-leisure-hive-reference', 'The Leisure Hive', 'Wikipedia contributors', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Leisure_Hive', 'secondary_tv_plot_reference_indexed', 'Public tourist business, bankruptcy and tachyon-generator passages read', 'A commercial leisure facility depends on tourist revenue and useful scientific work.', 'A leisure industry is not a whole resident post-work economy; impressive matter technology does not establish universal support.'),
    source('src-mysterious-planet-reference', 'The Mysterious Planet', 'Wikipedia contributors', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mysterious_Planet', 'secondary_tv_plot_reference_indexed', 'Public underground servants and demanded black-light repair passages read', 'Drathro commands people and requires useful technical maintenance.', 'Robotic authority is not sufficient evidence that the humans’ work is dispensable or that their necessities are independent of it.'),
